  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Masarouna</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Outline Description: What would you like to do? In Pathway 1, Masarouna&apos;s influencing efforts are aimed at addressing the immediate gaps in services, information and decision -making on Sexual and Reproductive Health Rights (SRHR) issues that concern Young People (YP) and demand accountability from decision -makers, health service providers and other stakeholders. Secondly the influencing efforts are aimed at changing harmful traditional social and cultural norms and values, countering misconceptions, misbeliefs, taboos and myths surrounding SRHR by providing accurate and up -to -date information and evidence on how current Sexual and Reproductive Health (SRH) norms and practices harm YP. Further, influencing efforts will highlight the positive social impact of meeting YPs&apos; SRHR needs. Pathway 2 is focused on strengthening civil society and reclaiming civic space. Interactions between governments/decision -makers, society and a strong civil society can lead to important societal transformations, but governments in the selected countries increasingly show authoritarian tendencies, restricting the space for engagement. Masarouna will therefore work with YP and the inclusion of YP in civil society, to strengthen their capacity to organise, build alliances and partnerships, deliver, lobby and advocate for their SRHR and opening up space for their voices.  Both pathways are supported by a cross -cutting capacity strengthening approach for YP and civil society actors. All partner organisations, formal and informal, networks and movements, involved in this programme bring separate knowledge, skills and networks to the table. Global and regional partners facilitate access to funds, bring in technical and thematic expertise, support on civic space, and broker opportunities to connect, and creates linkages between national, regional and global initiatives.</narrative>
  </description>
